#: ../../../file_formats/buildcache.rst:-1
msgid ""
"A developer reference for the layout of Spack build caches, describing its "
"structure, its compatibility across releases, and its version history."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/buildcache.rst:13
msgid "Build Cache Layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/buildcache.rst:15
msgid ""
"This document describes the build cache layout, which determines where "
"binary packages, their spec files, the index, and the public keys are stored "
"in a mirror. The current version of the layout is |"
"buildcache_layout_version|, defined by ``spack.url_buildcache."
"CURRENT_BUILD_CACHE_LAYOUT_VERSION``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/buildcache.rst:18
msgid ""
"The layout is used by build caches on a filesystem and on URLs such as "
"``https://`` and ``s3://``. Build caches in OCI registries do not use it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/buildcache.rst:22
msgid "Structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/buildcache.rst:24
msgid ""
"This section describes the current version of the layout, |"
"buildcache_layout_version|. A build cache has a directory of manifests, "
"named after the version of the layout, and a directory of blobs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/buildcache.rst:27
msgid ""
"<mirror>/\n"
"  v3/\n"
"    layout.json\n"
"    manifests/\n"
"      spec/\n"
"        zlib-ng/\n"
"          zlib-ng-2.3.3-nic37xsihlqze3xyg3xd6pthcgqxoy6p.spec.manifest.json\n"
"      index/\n"
"        index.manifest.json\n"
"      key/\n"
"        75BC0528114909C076E2607418010FFAD73C9B07.key.manifest.json\n"
"        keys.manifest.json\n"
"  blobs/\n"
"    sha256/\n"
"      0f/\n"
"        0f24aa6b5dd7150067349865217acd3f6a383083f9eca111d2d2fed726c88210"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/buildcache.rst:46
msgid ""
"``layout.json`` records how the build cache is signed, and its presence "
"indicates that the mirror has a build cache in this version of the layout. "
"Every other file, apart from the manifests, is stored as a blob named after "
"its checksum. A manifest lists the blobs that belong to one entity, which is "
"a binary package, the index, a public key, or the index of the public keys:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/buildcache.rst:50
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"version\": 3,\n"
"  \"data\": [\n"
"    {\n"
"      \"contentLength\": 10731083,\n"
"      \"mediaType\": \"application/vnd.spack.install.v2.tar+gzip\",\n"
"      \"compression\": \"gzip\",\n"
"      \"checksumAlgorithm\": \"sha256\",\n"
"      \"checksum\": "
"\"0f24aa6b5dd7150067349865217acd3f6a383083f9eca111d2d2fed726c88210\"\n"
"    },\n"
"    {\n"
"      \"contentLength\": 1000,\n"
"      \"mediaType\": \"application/vnd.spack.spec.v6+json\",\n"
"      \"compression\": \"gzip\",\n"
"      \"checksumAlgorithm\": \"sha256\",\n"
"      \"checksum\": "
"\"fba751c4796536737c9acbb718dad7429be1fa485f5585d450ab8b25d12ae041\"\n"
"    }\n"
"  ]\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/buildcache.rst:72
msgid "A manifest is a dictionary with the following keys:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/buildcache.rst:74
msgid "``version``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/buildcache.rst:75
msgid "The version of the layout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/buildcache.rst:76
msgid "``data``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/buildcache.rst:77
msgid ""
"One entry for each blob. ``checksumAlgorithm`` and ``checksum`` give the "
"location of the blob, which is ``blobs/<algorithm>/<first two characters of "
"the checksum>/<checksum>``. ``mediaType`` identifies the content of the blob "
"and the version of its format. ``compression`` is ``gzip`` or ``none``, and "
"``contentLength`` is the size of the blob in bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/buildcache.rst:82
msgid ""
"The manifest of a binary package can be signed, in which case the file is a "
"clearsigned document that contains the JSON above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/buildcache.rst:84
msgid "The media types tie the layout to the other formats:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats/buildcache.rst:86
msgid "Media types of the blobs"
msgstr ""

